      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "Point $A$ has coordinates $(3, 7)$. What is the position vector of $A$?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -7 \\end{pmatrix}$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$\\begin{pmatrix} 10 \\\\ 10 \\end{pmatrix}$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "The position vector of a point is the vector from the origin $O$ to that point. For $A(3, 7)$, the position vector is $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$."
